id|module|state|reason|cache|skip|origin|decision|unit|note
M1-01|m1|*|*|yes|*|*|charge|m1_cache|answered from the cache, full price: the answer is the value (flags.from_cache, M1-G3)
M1-02|m1|*|external_verified|no|*|*|charge|m1_vendor|the premium unit; reachable only when the owner switches the ZeroBounce fallback on (it ships disabled); only a vendor ANSWER carries this reason, a vendor non-answer leaves M1's own result standing and is charged by the ordinary rows, never as vendor
M1-03|m1|valid|accepted|no|*|*|charge|m1_own|a probed 2xx with no catch-all
M1-04|m1|valid|mailbox_full|no|*|*|charge|m1_own|452/552: the mailbox exists
M1-05|m1|invalid|no_mx|no|*|*|charge|m1_own|positive proof: no MX and no A/AAAA
M1-06|m1|invalid|null_mx|no|*|*|charge|m1_own|
M1-07|m1|invalid|spam_trap|no|*|*|charge|m1_own|
M1-08|m1|invalid|mailbox_not_found|no|*|*|charge|m1_own|550/551/553 with an address-fault body
M1-09|m1|invalid|historical_bounce|no|*|*|charge|m1_own|flywheel gate (off by default)
M1-10|m1|invalid|invalid_syntax|no|*|*|charge|m1_own|a bulk result since A1: M1 logs a malformed row and serves it as invalid/invalid_syntax, and the platform charges it like any settled answer (the platform no longer sends an address that fails norm/v1, row P-08; what still reaches this row is an address that module 1's syntax layer refuses after normalising it: a local part over 64 bytes, a domain over 255 bytes or a domain with no dot)
M1-11|m1|risky|disposable|no|*|*|charge|m1_own|
M1-12|m1|risky|provider_no_smtp|no|*|*|charge|m1_own|a settled answer: the provider is routed to MX-only by policy
M1-13|m1|risky|catch_all|no|*|*|charge|m1_own|
M1-14|m1|risky|non_public_mx|no|*|*|charge|m1_own|no probe was made, the verdict comes from DNS facts
M1-15|m1|risky|plausible|no|capacity|*|free||OUR capacity failure settled as risky/plausible (M1-G5): no node, audit red, warmup cap, rate limit; M1 also marks it failure_origin own
M1-16|m1|risky|plausible|no|none|*|charge|m1_own|no skip token: a cheap-layers answer
M1-17|m1|risky|plausible|no|smtp_unwired|*|free||SMTP was not wired at boot (skip token smtp_unwired): our configuration
M1-18|m1|unknown|greylisted|no|*|remote|charge|m1_own|retries exhausted: the recipient's server kept deferring
M1-19|m1|unknown|unknown_error|no|*|own|free||the attempt cap: a decrypt or compute error repeated to M1's cap, settled by M1 as unknown/unknown_error with origin own
M1-20|m1|unknown|*|no|*|remote|charge|m1_own|an unknown caused by the recipient's server
M1-21|m1|unknown|*|no|*|own|free||an unknown caused by us
M1-22|m1|unknown|*|no|*|undetermined|free||an unknown that cannot be proven either way
M1-23|m1|unknown|*|no|*|none|unmapped||an older module that does not name an origin: never charged, reported
M1-99|m1|*|*|*|*|*|unmapped||any other pair, including every reason the pinned module can legally name but never emits
M2-01|m2|sent|*|*|*|*|charge|m2_accepted|250 after DATA with a provider message id
M2-02|m2|bounced|*|*|*|*|charge|m2_bounced|550/551/553 at RCPT: the work was done, the bad address is the user's list (M2-G4: includes relay policy 550s)
M2-03|m2|failed|attempts_exhausted|*|*|*|free||the attempt cap or max age (B3): our failure
M2-04|m2|failed|*|*|*|*|free||any other failure, pool exhaustion included, keeps its own reason: our failure
M2-05|m2|queued|*|*|*|*|notfinal||not final: a retryable failure stays queued until it sends, bounces or reaches the attempt cap
M2-06|m2|assigned|*|*|*|*|notfinal||
M2-07|m2|sending|*|*|*|*|notfinal||
M2-08|m2|cancelled|*|*|*|*|free||cancelled before it was claimed (B4): work not done
M2-99|m2|*|*|*|*|*|unmapped||a state the pinned module does not define
M3-01|m3|*|*|*|*|*|free||module 3 is not metered: entitlements, not credits
P-01|platform|cancelled|*|*|*|*|free||cancelled by the user or an admin: work not done
P-02|platform|expired|*|*|*|*|free||a scheduled job or entitlement expired: work not done
P-03|platform|quarantined|*|*|*|*|free||quarantined by the platform: work not done
P-04|platform|infrastructure_failure|*|*|*|*|free||our own failure (module outage, platform crash window)
P-05|platform|pool_exhausted|*|*|*|*|free||no sending capacity: our own failure
P-06|platform|smtp_login_rejected|*|*|*|*|free||the user's own SMTP rejected the login: nothing reached the outside world
P-07|platform|duplicate|*|*|*|*|free||a repeat of an earlier row's address inside one M1 job: checked once, charged once, on the first row (internal/adapters/m1 maps duplicate_of rows to this state)
P-08|platform|malformed|*|*|*|*|free||an address that fails norm/v1 (internal/norm): counted and skipped before any module call, never sent and never charged (module 1's own invalid_syntax row M1-10 stays for completeness)
